From 57a73059ec1e6c4a18f0e99019e609f93b31fe53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(terminal): background spawns get the foreground's Hermes
 PATH dirs; flag masked missing commands [daveey]

Background terminal commands built PATH via _terminal_env(_sanitize_subprocess_env(...)),
which never appended the sane / Hermes-managed ($HERMES_HOME/bin, pm node) / ~/.local/bin
dirs that the foreground _make_run_env adds. On a systemd gateway (hermes-hub) whose
service PATH lacks ~/.hermes/bin, terminal(background=true) could not find hermes-core-wt
while the foreground could (self-heal defect agent-dab059c232).

- _terminal_env now applies _user_tools_first(_append_missing_sane_path_entries(...)),
  the same composition as _make_run_env (pipe and PTY spawns both use it).
- terminal_hints: missing-command shapes ("command not found", "failed to run command
  'x': No such file", env/nice/timeout ENOENT) count as failure shapes, so an exit-0
  `... | tail` over them gets the masked-success hint.
- process_manage poll/wait/log exited-0 results get the same hint.

Tests: tests/tools/test_background_spawn_path_parity.py (red on main), new
TestMaskedMissingCommand / TestProcessResultMaskedHint in test_terminal_hints.py.
